{
  "case_id": "2010-09-11121",
  "document_hash": "73adbfd3886b7662150cc44056d875aca6ae28cdd1246fc4452b2f4fde68c1d9",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11121",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73adbfd3886b7662150cc44056d875aca6ae28cdd1246fc4452b2f4fde68c1d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73adbfd3886b-0000-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nBARBARA S. BLACKMAN, ESQ., Durham, North Carolina; on behalf of Petitioner.\nROY COOPER, ESQ., Attorney General, Raleigh, North Carolina; on behalf of Respondent.\nERIC J. FEIGIN, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11121",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73adbfd3886b7662150cc44056d875aca6ae28cdd1246fc4452b2f4fde68c1d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73adbfd3886b-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We will hear argument next in Case 09-11121, J.D.B. v. North Carolina."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11121",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73adbfd3886b7662150cc44056d875aca6ae28cdd1246fc4452b2f4fde68c1d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73adbfd3886b-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "J.D.B. was only 13 years old when he was taken out of his middle school classroom and escorted to a closed door interrogation conducted by outside law enforcement regarding a matter that did not take place on school property."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11121",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73adbfd3886b7662150cc44056d875aca6ae28cdd1246fc4452b2f4fde68c1d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73adbfd3886b-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Ms. Blackman, I'm -- I'm -- I'm not clear on what you are proposing. Is there to be one different Miranda requirement rule for all minors, or is there to be one for, what, 20-year-olds, 19-year-olds, 18-year-olds, 17, 16? This one is 13, do we calibrate it that finely -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11121",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73adbfd3886b7662150cc44056d875aca6ae28cdd1246fc4452b2f4fde68c1d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73adbfd3886b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The way you phrase the question, you say, may the trial -- whether trial courts may consider the juvenile's age in Miranda to make the in-custody Miranda determination."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. BLACKMAN",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11121",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73adbfd3886b7662150cc44056d875aca6ae28cdd1246fc4452b2f4fde68c1d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73adbfd3886b-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No, it is must. As with any objective circumstance, the court has to take it into account, and we can't be relegating some to a discretionary review and others to mandatory review. So, yes, if a child is involved in the case, then a court must take that into account -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE BREYER",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11121",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73adbfd3886b7662150cc44056d875aca6ae28cdd1246fc4452b2f4fde68c1d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73adbfd3886b-0001-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, what happens to destroy the criminal justice system? You can see from my overstatement, I tend to suspect nothing, but you tell me. MR. COOPER: A lot. School resource officers, there are thousands of them, they are -- they are licensed, but police officers -- uniform police officers who often counsel kids as well as protect the school. Under the Petitioner's theory, a school resource officer who is going to take a juvenile into a room to talk about a stolen cell phone or bullying, the first thing that he's got to say is you have the right to remain silent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11121",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73adbfd3886b7662150cc44056d875aca6ae28cdd1246fc4452b2f4fde68c1d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73adbfd3886b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For search purposes, is age consciousness required? Remember, a part of this is the police officer then goes to the boy's home."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11121",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73adbfd3886b7662150cc44056d875aca6ae28cdd1246fc4452b2f4fde68c1d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73adbfd3886b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, you know, you want to talk -- you want to talk to the kid. If you have a traffic stop, you don't want to immediately tell the 15-year-old driver, you're free to leave, because he's not. It's just like Berkemer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11121",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73adbfd3886b7662150cc44056d875aca6ae28cdd1246fc4452b2f4fde68c1d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73adbfd3886b-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, do you agree with the solicitor general's view that a blind person should be treated as a blind person for -- for these purposes?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11121",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73adbfd3886b7662150cc44056d875aca6ae28cdd1246fc4452b2f4fde68c1d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73adbfd3886b-0002-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are three primary reasons why age should not be a factor in the Miranda custody test. think the most important one is this: The only statements that are going to be suppressed under Petitioner's rule that wouldn't already be suppressed by existing doctrine are statements that, first of all, the prosecution has -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Counsel",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11121",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73adbfd3886b7662150cc44056d875aca6ae28cdd1246fc4452b2f4fde68c1d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73adbfd3886b-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "request that the North Carolina Supreme Court decision be upheld."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11121",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73adbfd3886b7662150cc44056d875aca6ae28cdd1246fc4452b2f4fde68c1d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73adbfd3886b-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think what's very odd in this case is that the only party that didn't consider J.D.B.'s age was the courts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11121",
      "confidence": 0.0,
